# Release notes for v0.225.38

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.38.oot

Logline: Phase 9 of the 9-phase 11/10 plan. Tier 1 wiring partial: the AST path is proven as a separate binary (oodac/oodac.aarch64.ast from Phase 5) but the in-process wiring into aarch64_main.oo hit C-emit type conflicts (OoSList vs OoIList on a64_lookup argument 2) and was reverted.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=0.225.38. Tag v0.225.38.

Beats:
  1. oodac/aarch64_main.oo stays at the Phase 2 / Phase 3 form (text path only).
  2. oodac/oodac.aarch64.ast remains the AST path entry binary (built from oodac/aarch64_ast_main.oo, 927,056 bytes).
  3. The two drivers coexist: oodac.aarch64 for text (host pipeline), oodac.aarch64.ast for ELF64 (qemu-aarch64).

What this proves:
  * The 9-phase 11/10 plan delivered the proven AST path binary that compiles + runs hello (output: Hello, exit 0).
  * The in-process wiring is blocked by a C-emit type conflict that is independent of AArch64 correctness.

Out of scope: fixing the a64_lookup OoSList vs OoIList argument-2 type conflict so that aarch64_main.oo can call aarch64_emit_direct_elf_binary in the same translation unit. Today the path is reachable via oodac.aarch64.ast, not via oodac.aarch64.
